\subsection{C3: Certified Clock Profiling}
\label{subsec:res_c3}
Table~\ref{tab:c3_control} isolates Phase~II using $100$ shared
MKSC-GI initializers. CCOP-JVP and the range-scaled $c_0\Delta t$
4D-JVP control agree in conditional position and clock RMSE to the
reported precision.

Expressing the explicit clock coordinate in seconds increases conditional
position RMSE by $32\%$ in this control. The implemented CCOP-JVP route
returns bit-identical outputs under all three unit labels, consistent
with the mathematical unit invariance of Theorem~\ref{thm:clock}(ii).
Its outer dimension falls from four to three and median evaluations
from $13$ to $9$.

All $950$ conditional clock profiles meet the prescribed objective-gap
tolerance, with a worst gap/tolerance ratio of $0.998$ and no subdivision-cap
hit, which certifies the inner maximization at each visited position but
not the outer search. A larger independently seeded audit is supplementary.

